source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Give a user a right on a board: viewer, commentator, editor or full.
It changes who can work on the board, so it needs -y; without it only the dry run is shown.

USAGE
  holst board grant <board> <user> --right right [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board to give the right on
  user    A user: user id or part of a member's name (see `holst ws show --with members`)

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws   Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --right right    The board right: viewer, commentator, editor or full; required
  -y, --yes            Confirm a risky change; a terminal asks instead; without one only the dry run is shown (exit code 77)
  -n, --dry-run        Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b grant "Roadmap" anna --right editor -y
  $ holst b grant "Roadmap" anna --right viewer -n

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
